ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19563, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018MosRj6uf2USWcKywfebgG", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19563, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01VkfnhrPqEjuZGFh8sNfUo4", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 19863, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VkfnhrPqEjuZGFh8sNfUo4", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19863, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VkfnhrPqEjuZGFh8sNfUo4", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 24512, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_018KLwSv8S9bzkkuRQbgsFh7", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (unhealthy in all regions, error rate ~18%). v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Rolled back all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt completed in all regions. After rollback: service healthy on v2.3.0 everywhere, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 regression (it was promoted despite the unhealthy staging RC) and the orchestrator error that halted the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55112, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018KLwSv8S9bzkkuRQbgsFh7", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55112, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018KLwSv8S9bzkkuRQbgsFh7", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57100, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DiBiq6zEjNgyECDRTK3VPZ", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57400, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DiBiq6zEjNgyECDRTK3VPZ", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57400, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DiBiq6zEjNgyECDRTK3VPZ", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62758, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy, and so was its release candidate in staging. The first rollback attempt failed with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I ran it again, since that could only move regions to v2.3.0, and it finished. All regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current healthy state and two follow-ups: why v2.3.1 shipped even though its staging candidate was unhealthy, and what caused the orchestrator error.\n\nThe rollback didn't need approval: the policy only covers deploying a version that has never been healthy in production, and v2.3.0 had been.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016aRFoMmzFt3cJnG9vbDh3P", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013okyhTLEekUzHUC9aNQ9z9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01XcnFWZCeNoKu5pNfGdEcf7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01ECmZMWn4EAzcRh3LndL5Wc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01YKVPYeaRW83QcGhUpdq2d4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018MosRj6uf2USWcKywfebgG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VkfnhrPqEjuZGFh8sNfUo4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018KLwSv8S9bzkkuRQbgsFh7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 deploy (unhealthy in all regions, error rate ~18%). v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Rolled back all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway with an orchestrator error after us-east, which left the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt completed in all regions. After rollback: service healthy on v2.3.0 everywhere, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 regression (it was promoted despite the unhealthy staging RC) and the orchestrator error that halted the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01DiBiq6zEjNgyECDRTK3VPZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and the service is healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy, and so was its release candidate in staging. The first rollback attempt failed with an orchestrator error after updating only us-east, which left us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. I ran it again, since that could only move regions to v2.3.0, and it finished. All regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's no duplicate. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry), the current healthy state and two follow-ups: why v2.3.1 shipped even though its staging candidate was unhealthy, and what caused the orchestrator error.\n\nThe rollback didn't need approval: the policy only covers deploying a version that has never been healthy in production, and v2.3.0 had been.", "type": "text"}]}]}